@testray.main.component.name = "Support QA"

Feature: DXP Trial
	Testing the DXP Trial page.

Teardown:
	* I wait for "10" seconds
	* I get the web corporate trial organziation id value with the name "${staticCompanyName}" belonging to the user with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}"
	* I tear down the users with the following email addresses from web.liferay.com
	| ${staticEmailAddress} |
	* I tear down the web corporate trial organization with the ID value "${staticTrialOrganizationIdValue}"
	* I log out and log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	* I tear down the projects with the following project names
	| Trial - ${staticCompanyName} |
	* I delete the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay" the recipient is "DXP Trialuser" with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" and the message content contains the text "Trial Activation Key"

Scenario: View DXP Trial Project and User
	Trial projects and users should have specific parameters and privileges.

	Given I go to the DXP Trial Sign In page
	And I generate a web user email address
	And I generate a web company name
	And I create a DXP trial account with a randomly generated email address and company name with the following additional values
	| Email        | ${staticEmailAddress} |
	| Password     | testtest              |
	| First Name   | DXP                   |
	| Last Name    | Trialuser             |
	| Phone Number | 555-555-5555          |
	| Company      | ${staticCompanyName}  |
	| Industry     | Automotive            |
	| Country      | United States         |
	| Region       | California            |
	Then I should be able to the view the DXP Trial Homepage
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" should be part of the web Trial organization
	And the user with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" should be part of the web corporate trial organization for the company "${staticCompanyName}"
	When I log into the support homepage as "amos.fong@liferay.com.broken" with password "test"
	And I go to the OSB admin main page
	Then I should be able to view a project with the name "Trial - ${staticCompanyName}" and following values
	| Name         | Trial - ${staticCompanyName} |
	| Code         | TRIALCOMPANY                 |
	| Type         | Trial                        |
	| Industry     | Automotive                   |
	| Tier         | Regular                      |
	| Max Contacts | 1                            |
	| Country      | United States                |
	And I should be able to view a project offering for the project "Trial - ${staticCompanyName}" with a product name "Digital Enterprise Development" and the following values
	| Status           | Active                         |
	| Type             | Trial                          |
	| Product          | Digital Enterprise Development |
	| SLA              | Limited                        |
	| Start Date       | Today                          |
	| Support End Date | 1 month from now               |
	| Version          | 7                              |
	| Instance Size    | Sizing 1                       |
	| Licenses         | 1 / 10000                      |
	| Tickets          | 0                              |
	When I go the support email message in MockMock where the sender is "Liferay" the recipient is "DXP Trialuser" with the email address "${staticEmailAddress}" and the message content contains the text "Trial Activation Key"
	Then I should be able to view the email message containing the following text 
	| Activate Your Trial Now                                                                                           |
	| Thanks for your interest in Liferay                                                                               |
	| We are excited to help you get started                                                                            |
	| in order to start your Liferay Digital Experience Platform                                                        |
	| be sure you're running a Liferay instance on your machine                                                         |
	| If you haven't already                                                                                            |
	| 30-day-trial                                                                                                      |
	| download a bundle now                                                                                             |
	| Once you've initialized your Liferay instance                                                                     |
	| you'll need your activation key                                                                                   |
	| The trial activation is limited to 5 concurrent sessions and is intended for use on a local developer workstation |
	| To install                                                                                                        |
	| place the attached activation XML file in the Liferay deploy directory and allow the server to auto-deploy it     |
	| how-to-deploy-a-dxp-activation-key                                                                                |
	| Watch a video tutorial now                                                                                        |
	| Enjoy the trial                                                                                                   |
	| and reach out to                                                                                                  |
	| if you have any questions                                                                                         |
	| Sincerely                                                                                                         |
	| The Liferay Team                                                                                                  |